# Freeze the Gmail-parity MCP contract

## Goal

Define a stable provider-neutral tool surface before transport and adapter code
couple behavior to one implementation.

## Required work

- Specify message, thread, mailbox, label, draft, and attachment identifiers.
- Specify sender identities and reject unverified or unavailable From addresses.
- Specify search grammar, pagination, ordering, and time semantics.
- Specify unread/read state, archive/unarchive, trash/restore, draft discard,
  reply-all, mailbox event cursors, attachment bounds, and batch result shapes.
- Define structured errors and retryability.
- Assign MCP read-only, destructive, idempotent, and open-world annotations.
- Reconcile Proton behavior with the useful Gmail connector surface.

## Acceptance criteria

- Schemas round-trip through serialization tests.
- Pagination cannot silently duplicate or omit items under documented rules.
- Drafting and sending are separate tools.
- Every tool has a safety class and a capability requirement.
- The compatibility table identifies exact Gmail-surface parity, intentional
  differences, and capabilities unavailable on each adapter.
- The frozen inventory covers search/list/get message and thread, safe
  attachment retrieval, mailbox/label/sender listing, draft create/read/update/
  discard, send/reply/reply-all/forward, read state, label changes,
  archive/unarchive, move, trash/restore, and bounded change waiting.

## Evidence

- Versioned contract module
- Golden schema fixtures
- Compatibility table
